course: dictionary
lesson: 13871
title: Khmer: a people, a language and a history
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Khmer is a word with more than one meaning. It can name a people or a language, or it can describe things that belong to them. Read the words around it to find out which: «The Khmer Empire built the huge temple of Angkor Wat.» Here Khmer describes the empire, and it tells you which empire built the temple.
explain: Look at the words next to it too. «Many people in Cambodia speak Khmer.» People speak a language, so here Khmer names a language. Khmer always starts with a capital letter because it is the name of a people and their language.
explain: Be careful with «Khmer Rouge». It is the name of a cruel government that ruled Cambodia from 1975 to 1979 and killed very many people. The two words belong together as one name. This is a sad part of history, so ask a teacher or a grown-up if you want to learn more.
fact: Khmer can be a noun (a people, a language) or an adjective (it describes something).
fact: The Khmer people are the main people of Cambodia in South-East Asia.
fact: Khmer has its own alphabet, and it is one of the longest alphabets in the world.
fact: The Khmer Empire built Angkor Wat, a huge temple.
fact: The Khmer Rouge was a cruel government that ruled Cambodia from 1975 to 1979.
exercise: «Many people in Cambodia speak Khmer.» In this sentence, what does Khmer name? | A river in the hills | A king from long ago | A type of rice | *A language
exercise: «The Khmer Empire built the huge temple of Angkor Wat.» What does the word Khmer tell us? | A place to buy food | *Which empire built the temple | The name of a sports team | A kind of boat
exercise: «Khmer has one of the longest alphabets in the world.» What is Khmer in this sentence? | A kind of food | *The language, which has its own alphabet | A people who live in Europe | A very tall mountain
test: «The history book described the Khmer Rouge as a cruel government.» What does the Khmer Rouge describe? | A kind of festival | A river boat | *A cruel government that ruled Cambodia | A school club
test: Khmer is a word with more than one meaning. Which two things can it name? | A king and a queen | *A people and a language | A mountain and a lake | A sport and a food
exam: In «the Khmer script», what kind of word is Khmer? | A question word | *An adjective describing the script | A noun naming a people | A verb showing an action
